    whoUses: "Database engineers (every index is a B-tree), browser and compiler authors (the page and your code are parsed into trees), and file-system designers. The moment a problem involves hierarchy or ‘keep it sorted while I keep inserting', a tree is the answer — which is why interview questions on tree traversal are unavoidable.",
    bigPicture: "Trees are the bridge between data structures and the systems you've already learned. The B-tree index is *why* a database can find one row among millions instantly; the DOM tree is what React diffs to update a page; a router matches URLs by walking a tree. Master tree traversal and a huge amount of ‘how does that work?' suddenly clicks.",
    prereqs: ["linked-lists", "recursion-and-backtracking", "big-o-notation"],
